<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!--
	The functions of a project (haumacher/ehome #43): what the inhabitant operates on the HomeControl
	controller - a light, a dimmer, a blind, a sensor, a button -, each with the datapoints of the
	roles of its kind and its room. They are part of the runtime image (Deployment tab).

	"Propose functions" (de.haumacher.ehome.runtime.FunctionProposal) makes a candidate of each
	device channel from its own objects and links the candidates by the sending (first) group
	addresses of their objects into functions (haumacher/ehome #98): a key and the actuator channel
	receiving its address are one function, of the actuator's kind, named after the group address of
	its main role; a key no actuator receives is a button, a measured value a sensor. A channel
	whose main object has no group address gives an unused function, named "<device>: <channel>",
	without datapoints. Every function whose main role has no datapoint, also one the user made, is
	unused: the column "Unused" (and its filter) marks it, and the runtime image leaves it out and
	counts it in its summary. It adds the functions the project lacks, and a function for each application datapoint
	bound to a function of a Zigbee device (haumacher/ehome #68: a sensor, a switch or light, a
	dimmer), keyed by the device's IEEE address, the endpoint and the function. The only change it
	makes to an existing function: an unused one whose channel got its group address gets its
	datapoints, and a function whose name is still a generated one (the unused name, or the
	channel's name of earlier runs, "Kanal H") is renamed after its group address; a name the user
	edited and the datapoints the function binds stay. So it can run again after devices were added
	or linked. "New function" adds an empty one. The form of the selected function shows the roles
	of its kind only; the options of a role are the datapoints of the project, its group addresses
	and its application datapoints (haumacher/ehome #61).

	Deleting a proposed function remembers it as dismissed (haumacher/ehome #49), so the next proposal
	does not bring it back; the dismissed proposals are listed below the functions, and "Undo
	dismissal" (haumacher/ehome #99) deletes the dismissal, so the next proposal adds the function
	again.

	A button whose press is the command of another function (haumacher/ehome #92: a key operating an
	actuator's channel, which the proposal no longer makes a button) shows a warning in the column
	"Warning" and above its form (functionRedundancy, de.haumacher.ehome.runtime.FunctionProposal);
	the user deletes it. The same places warn about a role bound to a group address on which no object
	in effect does what the role needs: no object taking the command of a command role, none sending
	the value of any other role, e.g. because the object is switched off by its device's parameters
	(functionWarning, de.haumacher.ehome.runtime.FunctionRoleCheck, haumacher/ehome #137).

	Configuring by intent (haumacher/ehome #147): a function names the actuator preset of the template
	of its device's program that configures its channel ("Actuator preset", the presets offered on the
	channel); the table "Controls" below its form lists what operates it from where (a key, a rocker, a
	status LED of a device with its source preset and the operation), added in
	projects/control-create.view.xml and edited in the form below the table; a control the derivation
	refuses shows the reason. "Derive installation" computes the group addresses, connections and
	parameter values the functions and controls need (de.haumacher.ehome.intent.Derivation) and shows
	them in projects/derivation-preview.view.xml, which applies them; nothing changes before.
-->
<view>
	<channels>
		<channel name="project"/>
		<channel name="function"/>
		<channel name="dismissal"/>
		<!-- The selected control of the function (haumacher/ehome #147). -->
		<channel name="selectedControl"/>
		<derived-channel name="control"
			expr="if($function != null and $selectedControl != null and $function.get(`ehome.runtime:Function#controls`).containsElement($selectedControl), $selectedControl, null)"
			inputs="function, selectedControl"
			observed-types="ehome.runtime:Control"
		/>
		<!--
			Why the selected function is redundant on the controller, and its roles no object in effect
			serves; nothing if all is well.
		-->
		<derived-channel name="redundancy"
			expr="functionWarning($function)"
			inputs="function"
			observed-types="ehome.runtime:Function,ehome.physical:Connection,ehome.physical:Connector,ehome.physical:ParameterSetting"
		/>
		<!-- The name of this page for the assistant (app.view.xml, <page-selection> below). -->
		<derived-channel name="assistantPage"
			expr="'Project, tab Functions'"
		/>
	</channels>
	<split-panel
		orientation="horizontal"
		resizable="true"
	>
		<panes>
			<pane
				min-size="300"
				size="50"
				unit="%"
			>
				<!-- What the assistant is told about this page: its name and its selection (app.view.xml). -->
				<page-selection to="pageView">
					<inputs>
						<input channel="assistantPage"/>
					</inputs>
				</page-selection>
				<page-selection to="pageSelection">
					<inputs>
						<input channel="function"/>
						<input channel="dismissal"/>
						<input channel="project"/>
					</inputs>
				</page-selection>
				<split-panel
					orientation="vertical"
					resizable="true"
				>
					<panes>
						<pane
							size="70"
							unit="%"
						>
							<panel>
								<title>
									<en>Functions</en>
									<de>Funktionen</de>
								</title>
								<commands>
									<generic-command
										image="css:bi bi-magic"
										inputs="project"
										placement="TOOLBAR"
									>
										<label>
											<en>Propose functions</en>
											<de>Funktionen vorschlagen</de>
										</label>
										<tooltip>
											<en>Adds a function for every set of device channels linked by a group address, named after the address, and an unused one for every channel without a group address. Of existing functions, it only fills the roles of unused ones that got linked; edited names, bound roles and dismissed proposals stay.</en>
											<de>Legt für jede über eine Gruppenadresse verbundene Gruppe von Gerätekanälen eine Funktion mit dem Namen der Adresse an und für jeden Kanal ohne Gruppenadresse eine unbenutzte. An bestehenden Funktionen ergänzt er nur die Rollen unbenutzter, die inzwischen verbunden sind; bearbeitete Namen, gebundene Rollen und verworfene Vorschläge bleiben.</de>
										</tooltip>
										<access>
											<operation name="Write"
												object="$project"
												type="ehome.project:Project"
											/>
										</access>
										<executability>
											<null-input-disabled/>
										</executability>
										<propose-functions>
											<with-result>
												<notify
													expr="$result"
													kind="info"
												/>
											</with-result>
										</propose-functions>
									</generic-command>
									<!--
										The derivation of the group addresses, connections and parameter values from the
										functions with an actuator preset and their controls (haumacher/ehome #147): computed
										without changing anything and shown in projects/derivation-preview.view.xml, applied
										from there.
									-->
									<generic-command
										image="css:bi bi-diagram-3"
										inputs="project"
										placement="TOOLBAR"
									>
										<label>
											<en>Derive installation</en>
											<de>Installation ableiten</de>
										</label>
										<tooltip>
											<en>Shows what the functions with an actuator preset and their controls make of the installation: the group addresses, the connections and the parameter values to create, change and remove, and the controls refused with their reasons. Nothing changes before "Apply" in the preview.</en>
											<de>Zeigt, was die Funktionen mit einer Aktor-Voreinstellung und ihre Bedienstellen aus der Installation machen: die Gruppenadressen, Verbindungen und Parameterwerte, die angelegt, geändert und entfernt werden, und die abgelehnten Bedienstellen mit ihren Gründen. Vor „Anwenden“ in der Vorschau ändert sich nichts.</de>
										</tooltip>
										<access>
											<!-- The preview reads only (intentPreview); applying checks Write on the project. -->
											<operation name="Read"
												object="$project"
												type="ehome.project:Project"
											/>
										</access>
										<executability>
											<null-input-disabled/>
										</executability>
										<execute-script function="intentPreview($project)">
											<with-result>
												<open-dialog
													bind-input-to="request"
													dialog-view="projects/derivation-preview.view.xml"
												/>
											</with-result>
										</execute-script>
									</generic-command>
									<generic-command
										image="css:bi bi-plus-lg"
										inputs="project"
										placement="TOOLBAR"
									>
										<label>
											<en>New function</en>
											<de>Neue Funktion</de>
										</label>
										<access>
											<operation name="Write"
												object="$project"
												type="ehome.project:Project"
											/>
										</access>
										<executability>
											<null-input-disabled/>
										</executability>
										<create-function>
											<with-result>
												<write-channel name="function"/>
											</with-result>
										</create-function>
									</generic-command>
									<generic-command
										image="css:bi bi-trash"
										inputs="function"
										placement="TOOLBAR"
									>
										<label>
											<en>Delete</en>
											<de>Löschen</de>
										</label>
										<access>
											<operation name="Delete"
												object="$function"
												type="ehome.runtime:Function"
											/>
											<operation name="Write"
												object="$function"
												type="ehome.runtime:Function"
											/>
										</access>
										<executability>
											<delete-veto-disabled/>
											<null-input-disabled/>
										</executability>
										<confirm expr="if($function.get(`ehome.runtime:Function#channel`) == null, #('Delete the function {0}?'@en, 'Funktion {0} löschen?'@de), #('Delete the function {0}? The proposal will not add it again unless it is restored.'@en, 'Funktion {0} löschen? Der Vorschlag fügt sie nicht wieder hinzu, solange sie nicht zurückgeholt wird.'@de)).fill($function.get(`ehome.runtime:Function#name`))"/>
										<delete-function/>
										<write-channel name="function" clear="true"/>
									</generic-command>
								</commands>
								<table
									group-by="room"
									observed-types="ehome.runtime:Function"
									personalization-key="ehome-functions"
									selection="function"
									types="ehome.runtime:Function"
								>
									<presets>
										<preset name="used">
											<label>
												<en>In use</en>
												<de>Benutzt</de>
											</label>
											<criterion
												column="unused"
												expr="false"
											/>
										</preset>
										<preset name="unused"
											count="true"
										>
											<label>
												<en>Unused</en>
												<de>Unbenutzt</de>
											</label>
											<criterion
												column="unused"
												expr="true"
											/>
										</preset>
									</presets>
									<inputs>
										<input channel="project"/>
									</inputs>
									<columns>
										<column attribute="name"/>
										<column attribute="kind"/>
										<column attribute="unused"/>
										<column attribute="room"/>
										<column attribute="identifier"/>
										<column attribute="device"/>
										<column attribute="preset"/>
										<computed-column name="warning"
											type="tl.core:String"
											width="300"
										>
											<label>
												<en>Warning</en>
												<de>Warnung</de>
											</label>
											<value>functionWarning($row)</value>
										</computed-column>
									</columns>
									<rows>if($project == null, [], $project.get(`ehome.project:Project#functions`))</rows>
								</table>
							</panel>
						</pane>
						<pane
							size="30"
							unit="%"
						>
							<panel>
								<title>
									<en>Dismissed proposals</en>
									<de>Verworfene Vorschläge</de>
								</title>
								<commands>
									<generic-command
										image="css:bi bi-arrow-counterclockwise"
										inputs="dismissal"
										placement="TOOLBAR"
									>
										<label>
											<en>Undo dismissal</en>
											<de>Verwerfen aufheben</de>
										</label>
										<tooltip>
											<en>The next run of "Propose functions" proposes the function again.</en>
											<de>Der nächste Lauf von „Funktionen vorschlagen“ schlägt die Funktion wieder vor.</de>
										</tooltip>
										<executability>
											<null-input-disabled/>
										</executability>
										<delete-object/>
										<write-channel name="dismissal" clear="true"/>
										<notify
											expr="#('The next run of &quot;Propose functions&quot; adds the function again.'@en, 'Der nächste Lauf von „Funktionen vorschlagen“ fügt die Funktion wieder hinzu.'@de)"
											kind="info"
										/>
									</generic-command>
								</commands>
								<table
									observed-types="ehome.runtime:DismissedProposal"
									selection="dismissal"
									types="ehome.runtime:DismissedProposal"
								>
									<inputs>
										<input channel="project"/>
									</inputs>
									<columns>
										<column attribute="name"/>
										<column attribute="kind"/>
										<column attribute="device"/>
									</columns>
									<rows>if($project == null, [], $project.get(`ehome.project:Project#dismissedProposals`))</rows>
								</table>
							</panel>
						</pane>
					</panes>
				</split-panel>
			</pane>
			<pane
				size="50"
				unit="%"
			>
				<panel>
					<title>
						<en>Function</en>
						<de>Funktion</de>
					</title>
					<stack>
						<visible-if
							expr="$redundancy != null"
							input="redundancy"
						>
							<inset>
								<text
									input="redundancy"
									tone="warning"
								/>
							</inset>
						</visible-if>
						<form
							input="function"
							with-inset="true"
						>
							<field attribute="name"/>
							<field attribute="kind"/>
							<field attribute="preset"/>
							<field attribute="derivationProblem"/>
							<field attribute="unused"/>
							<field attribute="room"/>
							<field attribute="identifier"/>
							<field attribute="unit"/>
							<field attribute="scene"/>
							<group>
								<label>
									<en>Datapoints</en>
									<de>Datenpunkte</de>
								</label>
								<field attribute="command"/>
								<field attribute="state"/>
								<field attribute="levelCommand"/>
								<field attribute="level"/>
								<field attribute="step"/>
								<field attribute="move"/>
								<field attribute="stop"/>
								<field attribute="position"/>
								<field attribute="positionCommand"/>
								<field attribute="slat"/>
								<field attribute="slatCommand"/>
								<field attribute="atTop"/>
								<field attribute="atBottom"/>
								<field attribute="value"/>
								<field attribute="temperature"/>
								<field attribute="setpoint"/>
								<field attribute="setpointCommand"/>
								<field attribute="mode"/>
								<field attribute="modeCommand"/>
								<field attribute="heating"/>
								<field attribute="heatingLevel"/>
								<field attribute="press"/>
							</group>
							<group>
								<label>
									<en>Proposed for</en>
									<de>Vorgeschlagen für</de>
								</label>
								<field attribute="device"
									readonly="true"
								/>
							</group>
						</form>
						<panel>
							<title>
								<en>Controls</en>
								<de>Bedienstellen</de>
							</title>
							<commands>
								<generic-command
									image="css:bi bi-plus-lg"
									inputs="function"
									placement="TOOLBAR"
								>
									<label>
										<en>Add control</en>
										<de>Bedienstelle hinzufügen</de>
									</label>
									<tooltip>
										<en>Adds what operates the function from where: a key, a rocker or a status LED of a device with its source preset and the operation. "Derive installation" connects it.</en>
										<de>Fügt hinzu, was die Funktion von wo aus bedient: eine Taste, eine Wippe oder eine Status-LED eines Geräts mit ihrer Quell-Voreinstellung und der Bedienung. „Installation ableiten“ verbindet sie.</de>
									</tooltip>
									<access>
										<operation name="Write"
											object="$function"
											type="ehome.runtime:Function"
										/>
									</access>
									<executability>
										<null-input-disabled/>
									</executability>
									<open-dialog
										bind-input-to="function"
										dialog-view="projects/control-create.view.xml"
									>
										<bind
											channel="selection"
											to="selectedControl"
										/>
									</open-dialog>
								</generic-command>
								<generic-command
									image="css:bi bi-trash"
									inputs="control"
									placement="TOOLBAR"
								>
									<label>
										<en>Delete control</en>
										<de>Bedienstelle löschen</de>
									</label>
									<tooltip>
										<en>Deletes the control; the next derivation removes what it derived.</en>
										<de>Löscht die Bedienstelle; die nächste Ableitung entfernt, was sie abgeleitet hat.</de>
									</tooltip>
									<access>
										<operation name="Delete"
											object="$control"
											type="ehome.runtime:Control"
										/>
									</access>
									<executability>
										<null-input-disabled/>
									</executability>
									<delete-object/>
									<write-channel name="selectedControl"
										clear="true"
									/>
								</generic-command>
							</commands>
							<stack>
								<table
									observed-types="ehome.runtime:Control,ehome.runtime:Function,ehome.runtime:DerivedPart,ehome.template:Preset"
									selection="selectedControl"
									types="ehome.runtime:Control"
								>
									<inputs>
										<input channel="function"/>
									</inputs>
									<columns>
										<column attribute="channelName"
											width="160"
										/>
										<column attribute="device"
											width="180"
										/>
										<column attribute="preset"
											width="160"
										/>
										<column attribute="operation"
											width="120"
										/>
										<column attribute="problem"
											width="300"
										/>
									</columns>
									<rows>if($function == null, [], $function.get(`ehome.runtime:Function#controls`))</rows>
								</table>
								<form
									input="control"
									with-inset="true"
								>
									<field attribute="device"
										readonly="true"
									/>
									<field attribute="channelName"/>
									<field attribute="preset"/>
									<field attribute="operation"/>
									<field attribute="problem"/>
								</form>
							</stack>
						</panel>
					</stack>
				</panel>
			</pane>
		</panes>
	</split-panel>
</view>
